+# Preview preflight incident — correction UNAPPLIED
+
+Base/reviewed installation: `972dc257f75c3f88087c49feda803af9e3bc7b7c`.
+Run43518878650, job132207896171, attempt1, existing workflow409607134,
+owner58099771, branch `native-pilot/private-beta-rc`. This document neither
+reuses that approval/window nor authorizes another run.
+
+## Established evidence and limits
+
+- The job log records successful public dependency installation, build, encryption
+  and both artifact transfers. The invocation step emitted only the original generic
+  `NATIVE_PREVIEW_HOLD`, at2026-11-13T22:27:11Z (4:27PM CST).
+- GitHub metadata reports original preserved artifact14081208632 and held
+  artifact14081428110, each53,601,765 ZIP bytes, same digest
+  `cf98cff2c60d553e114b0d40d0d3980fddc7f4ea20abac0c5079c6bd870358de`.
+  The founder independently verified ZIP bytes and the two-file inventory:
+  `build.aesgcm`, `receipt.json`; no `attempt.jsonl` or `binding.json`.
+  Workspace transfer of the relay's signed file reference was unavailable; this
+  investigation does not claim a separate local ZIP-byte verification. No decryption
+  or archive-key read was attempted. Hosted originals/retention are unchanged.
+- The saved approval API record exactly matches owner User58099771, approved,
+  environment26516929095 and the expected complete approval comment ending
+  `1794609960000`. Known run identity fields match the compiled requirements.
+  This does not establish which responses the workflow's reader actually received.
+- The original uploader writes/fsyncs a journal before its sole Vercel invocation
+  and contains no journal deletion. Given the verified complete held inventory and
+  unchanged code, its failure is before that invocation (including a possible failure
+  opening the journal). This is specific to this uploader; it is not a statement
+  about unrelated actors, platform metadata, or original publisher run42293408658.
+- No endpoint, HTTP status or failing predicate was logged. The elapsed2.4seconds
+  does not identify the number of requests or service. Connector404/403 evidence
+  is unrelated to the workflow token's response and is not used as its substitute.
+
+## Reproduced defect; historical first failure remains UNKNOWN
+
+The original requests `/v1/integrations/installations?teamId=...` and requires
+`configs.configurations`. Vercel documents the listing as
+`/v1/integrations/configurations?view=account&teamId=...`, returning an **array**.
+The pinned CLI64.5 also uses the configurations API (v2) and treats it as an array.
+References:
+
+- https://vercel.com/docs/rest-api/integrations/get-configurations-for-the-authenticated-user-or-team
+- https://vercel.com/docs/rest-api/sdk/examples/integrations
+
+Committed tests execute the original code unchanged and show that the documented
+array cannot pass its integration gate. The correction uses the documented v1
+listing and applies the original no-global/no-applicable-project condition to
+either that array or the previously accepted wrapper. It adds a1000-entry bound
+and conservatively holds empty/malformed/all-project or unknown selection scope.
+Null/missing project scope, applicable installations, pagination, denied/uncertain
+reads and unknown bodies still HOLD. No installation-type filter hides handlers.
+
+This is a genuine independent API-contract defect, **not proof that this run
+reached it**. Earlier project/Node/Git/protection/alias predicates, GitHub/Vercel
+HTTP/permission/token-format failures, local Git/link/output pins and journal-open
+failure remain possible. The exact earliest failing predicate cannot be recovered
+from the existing generic message. No credential replacement is proposed.
+
+## Minimal correction and diagnostics
+
+- Shared GET preflight; original uploader API/re-exports and deployment argv retained.
+- Each existing verification predicate is labeled; an AST-based test compares all
+ 22 original guard groups, preserving their expressions/order. Owner/reviewer/bypass,
+ branch, time, project, protection, alias, immutable identity and source-OFF gates
+ are not removed or relaxed.
+- Failed reads emit only a fixed endpoint label, categorical reason and numeric
+ HTTP status where available; logical failures name a fixed predicate. Examples:
+ `VC_PROJECT/http_status/403`, `PROJECT_NODE_VERSION`, `OWNER_REVIEW_EXACT_COMMENT`,
+ `INTEGRATIONS_SCOPE`. No URL, body, header value, token fragment/hash, key, error
+ message or stack is logged. Unknown exceptions get a fixed category.
+- `cliState` describes only the corrected invocation: `not_started`,
+ `started_unconfirmed` or `acknowledged`. This is not retroactive evidence about
+ the original run. Existing journals and uncertain/lost acknowledgments remain
+ fail-closed and cannot retry. Legacy HOLD output is retained.
+- No application/lib/SQL/policy/toolchain-lock/auth/source/STOP/collector/manual
+ workflow body is changed. The existing CI scope command is routed to a finite
+ additive review, replaying the original972 reviewer and tests unchanged. The
+ additional CI definition is offline/no-SQL/no-secrets; it is not a live inspector.
+
+## Critical advisory: retained, not upgraded
+
+A fresh audit of the unchanged tool lock reproduces36 findings:15moderate,
+20high,1critical. The original log has identical counts but no archived advisory
+JSON, so this identification uses the pinned lock and current npm advisory data.
+
+- Affected `tar@7.5.11`; critical finding
+  https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-23hp-3jrh-7fpw
+  (unbounded decompression/parse resource exhaustion; reported affected<=7.5.18).
+- Paths: `vercel@64.5.0 -> @vercel/container@19.1.3 -> tar@7.5.11`, and deduped
+  through `@vercel/backends -> @vercel/nft -> @mapbox/node-pre-gyp`.
+  `@vercel/fun` separately resolves `tar@7.5.22`; do not conflate the copies.
+- Container tar extraction occurs in `fetchPinnedArchive`/`fetchBuildpackage`
+  (including OCI layers). The native-addon chain extracts archives during binary
+  installation/test packaging. `npm ci --ignore-scripts` is already required.
+- The uploader's pre-invocation path is JSON/hash/Git/native-HTTPS validation.
+  Its actual pinned Git-metadata helper and import-only deploy-module probe load
+  no vulnerable root tar parser. The command itself is **not executed** by this
+  investigation. The GET-only inspector has no CLI/SDK import at all.
+- The reviewed Build Output validator accepts only Node24/edge functions, not
+  container build inputs. This finding cannot explain the observed pre-invocation
+  HOLD. No affected parse path was found for the fixed ordinary prebuilt Next
+  upload; this is a scoped static/import assessment, not a proof for every CLI
+  branch or a genuine hosted upload. Expanding commands, accepting container inputs
+  or parsing untrusted archives requires renewed review.
+
+The advisory remains in the toolchain. No upgrade/override/audit-fix was run.
+Policy/tool package/lock hashes remain byte-identical. An upgrade requires a
+separate dependency review and new builder/CLI pins, never an automatic repair.
+
+## Proposed next observation — GET ONLY, separate owner GO
+
+`inspect-only.mjs` has **no main/execute entry and is not wired into any workflow**.
+Its bound production reader uses native TLS and only fixed GitHub/Vercel GETs.
+It imports no uploader, CLI or child_process. Offline tests prove protocol
+separation: its manifest cannot authorize the uploader; a Preview GO cannot
+authorize inspection. Every outcome is `HOLD_NO_DEPLOYMENT_AUTHORITY`, activate:false.
+
+The proposed job would reuse existing `native-pilot-setup`, sole-owner review,
+no admin bypass, exact branch and the existing two read/upload-token bindings.
+**Do not bind the archive key.** No new secret, environment or permission is needed.
+Use a distinct new actual run/approval, exact reviewed diagnostic SHA, attempt1,
+an owner-selected validity interval<=5minutes, version `native-preview-inspection/1`,
+maxRequests9, deploy:false, sourceGo:false, sql:false, archiveKey:false. No execution
+interval is selected here. This does not start a30-minute deployment window.
+
+Exactly one request per path, sequential; <=9 total,4seconds/request,1MiB/256chunks
+per response, no redirect, pagination, retry or arbitrary path:
+
+1. Actual diagnostic run metadata.
+2. Saved setup-environment protection metadata.
+3. Exact setup-environment branch policy.
+4. Actual diagnostic run approval history.
+5. Pinned Vercel project identity/Node/Git/protection metadata.
+6. Complete bounded project aliases.
+7. Project webhooks.
+8. Documented account-view integration configurations.
+9. Legacy integration URL for categorical status/shape comparison only, after
+   all prior controls pass. Never a fallback authorization source.
+
+Stops on an earlier failed control. Final legacy comparison cannot confer any
+authority. The transport never reads secret-value or private-manifest endpoints, uses no
+bypass and prints no response values. A future approved job's fixed wrapper would
+call `runReadOnlyInspection` and print its sanitized result; it must catch any
+constructor error with `reportFailure`, never a raw exception.
+
+**Before any such dispatch**, independently review its feature-ref workflow
+wiring. A new inspection mode must be excluded from BOTH legacy context/publish
+jobs AND the Preview upload jobs, use the existing protected setup environment,
+and require this distinct exact comment:
+
+`APPROVE_NATIVE_PREFLIGHT_GET_ONLY <actualRun> <reviewedSHA> <projectID> <expiryMillis>`.
+
+Do not dispatch `preview-output` as a diagnostic. No old run retry, old approval
+reuse, variable deletion, metadata cleanup, key/token rotation or upload is allowed.
+GitHub's automatic environment-job record must be disclosed in that separate GO;
+no explicit publisher deployment/status POST is permitted. The proposed record is
+read-only evidence, never setup/source authorization or an upload approval.
+
+## Validation and delivery boundary
+
+Run the focused baseline regression, new predicate/transport/redaction/inspection
+tests, real loopback native TLS/SNI test, typecheck, lint, production build and
+archive check with existing local-only/no-database guards. No SQL is run.
+Original full native/PG CI evidence for972 is not claimed as a new patched-head run.
+
+This correction is delivered as a local, unapplied patch/commit only. It has not
+been pushed, installed or dispatched. No hosted setting changed. `vercel.json`
+and the installed release ref remain unchanged. A future publication/install
+needs separately reviewed trigger suppression; do not push an unregistered
+diagnostic topic branch and accidentally request a Git Preview.
+
+Preserve both original artifacts, receipts, approval and run history, including
+the independent42293408658 incident's UNKNOWN historical write disposition.
+This work authorizes neither a restore nor source acquisition.
